{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.PretzelRemainderFromPtolemy","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.PretzelRemainderFromPtolemy","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Order.IntermediateValue","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FloorRemainderFromDerivedShapeFields"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PretzelRemainderFromPtolemy.pretzel_pk_and_remainder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PretzelRemainderFromPtolemy.pretzel_pk_and_remainder","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PretzelRemainderFromPtolemy.lean#L109-L111","doc":"`|P_K| = 7` and remainder `4`, now with a derived source on all three knots. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PretzelRemainderFromPtolemy.pretzel_realEmbeddings_derived","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PretzelRemainderFromPtolemy.pretzel_realEmbeddings_derived","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PretzelRemainderFromPtolemy.lean#L99-L107","doc":"**The transcribed pretzel row is the derived count**: `4 = 3 + 1` real\nembeddings — three real roots of the class-0 cubic, one of the class-1 cubic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PretzelRemainderFromPtolemy.realCubic_three_real_roots","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PretzelRemainderFromPtolemy.realCubic_three_real_roots","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PretzelRemainderFromPtolemy.lean#L75-L97","doc":"**Three real roots**, one in each of `(−3,−2)`, `(−2,−1)`, `(−1,1)` — the\nintermediate value theorem three times; the intervals are disjoint, so the roots\nare distinct. A cubic has no more, so this is the full signature `(3, 0)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PretzelRemainderFromPtolemy.realCubic_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PretzelRemainderFromPtolemy.realCubic_one","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PretzelRemainderFromPtolemy.lean#L73-L73","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PretzelRemainderFromPtolemy.realCubic_neg_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PretzelRemainderFromPtolemy.realCubic_neg_one","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PretzelRemainderFromPtolemy.lean#L72-L72","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PretzelRemainderFromPtolemy.realCubic_neg_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PretzelRemainderFromPtolemy.realCubic_neg_two","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PretzelRemainderFromPtolemy.lean#L71-L71","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PretzelRemainderFromPtolemy.realCubic_neg_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PretzelRemainderFromPtolemy.realCubic_neg_three","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PretzelRemainderFromPtolemy.lean#L70-L70","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PretzelRemainderFromPtolemy.realCubic_continuous","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PretzelRemainderFromPtolemy.realCubic_continuous","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc